---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About — ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="About CircuitHub — AI-assisted electronics hardware development." />
		<style>
			.about-hero {
				text-align: center;
				padding: 4em 0 3em;
			}
			.about-hero h1 {
				font-size: 2.8em;
				font-weight: 800;
				margin-bottom: 0.5em;
			}
			.about-hero .accent {
				background: var(--gradient-1);
				-webkit-background-clip: text;
				-webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
				background-clip: text;
			}
			.about-hero p {
				max-width: 560px;
				margin: 0 auto;
				font-size: 1.1em;
				color: var(--text-secondary);
			}

			.about-content {
				max-width: 680px;
				margin: 0 auto;
			}
			.about-content h2 {
				font-size: 1.4em;
				font-weight: 600;
				margin: 2em 0 0.75em;
				color: var(--text-primary);
			}
			.about-content p {
				margin-bottom: 1.2em;
				color: var(--text-secondary);
				line-height: 1.7;
			}

			.topics-grid {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
				gap: 1em;
				margin: 1.5em 0;
			}
			.topic-card {
				background: var(--bg-card);
				border: 1px solid var(--border);
				border-radius: var(--radius);
				padding: 1.25em;
				transition: all 0.3s ease;
			}
			.topic-card:hover {
				border-color: rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.15);
				background: var(--bg-card-hover);
			}
			.topic-card .icon {
				font-size: 1.5em;
				margin-bottom: 0.5em;
			}
			.topic-card h3 {
				font-size: 1em;
				font-weight: 600;
				margin: 0 0 0.4em;
				color: var(--text-primary);
			}
			.topic-card p {
				font-size: 0.9em;
				margin: 0;
				color: var(--text-muted);
			}

			@media (max-width: 720px) {
				.about-hero h1 {
					font-size: 2em;
				}
				.topics-grid {
					grid-template-columns: 1fr;
				}
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="about-hero">
				<h1>
					About <span class="accent">CircuitHub</span>
				</h1>
				<p>
					Exploring the intersection of artificial intelligence and electronics hardware
					engineering — one KiCad project at a time.
				</p>
			</section>

			<div class="about-content">
				<p>
					CircuitHub is a blog dedicated to pushing the boundaries of electronics hardware
					development using AI. I believe that artificial intelligence — from large language
					models to specialized ML tools — can fundamentally change how we design, simulate,
					and manufacture electronic circuits.
				</p>

				<h2>What I Write About</h2>

				<div class="topics-grid">
					<div class="topic-card">
						<div class="icon">🧠</div>
						<h3>AI-Assisted Design</h3>
						<p>Using LLMs and AI agents to accelerate schematic capture, PCB layout, and design reviews.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="topic-card">
						<div class="icon">⚡</div>
						<h3>KiCad + AI</h3>
						<p>Extending KiCad capabilities for larger teams — automation, scripting, and intelligent routing.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="topic-card">
						<div class="icon">🔄</div>
						<h3>Workflow Automation</h3>
						<p>Streamlining the hardware development pipeline from spec to BOM to manufacturing.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="topic-card">
						<div class="icon">🔬</div>
						<h3>Team-Scale Hardware</h3>
						<p>Best practices for collaborative hardware design, version control, and CI/CD for electronics.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<h2>Why This Blog?</h2>
				<p>
					Hardware development has lagged behind software in tooling and automation. With the
					rise of capable AI models, we now have an opportunity to close that gap. This blog
					documents experiments, workflows, and tools that make electronics engineering faster,
					smarter, and more collaborative.
				</p>
				<p>
					Whether you're a solo hardware hacker or part of a growing team, if you're curious
					about how AI can supercharge your electronics workflow — you're in the right place.
				</p>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
